# B16, BF16, B32, B64 and B128 `rsqrt_unchecked` round correctly: 1 / sqrt(x) rounded once to nearest (ties to
# even). Every B16 and BF16 bit pattern, every 4093th B32 pattern (wrapping, 1048576 of them) plus the
# inputs CORE-MATH corrects by hand, the B64 and B128 worst cases of CORE-MATH (rsqrt.wc, part of rsqrtq.wc) plus
# powers of two, subnormals and random patterns. Each type folds its results into a checksum (a NaN counts as one
# value), and rsqrt.expected holds the checksums of the exact results, computed with integer square roots.

